    "summary_one_sentence": "In 1859, a widowed doctor must transport a freed slave and her deadly, cursed daughter across the perilous American West to seek a remote faith healer.",
    "summary_short": "Set during the summer of 1859, a grieving, widowed physician reluctantly embarks on a five-day trek across a violent frontier. He is tasked with escorting a recently freed slave and her enigmatic Caucasian child, who possesses a terrifying affliction: any living thing she touches instantly dies. While the mother believes her child is demonically possessed, the skeptical doctor suspects a rare medical illness, forcing them to journey together toward a distant faith healer in a desperate bid for answers.",
    "summary_long": "Against the backdrop of the American West in 1859, a grieving widowed physician finds his rational worldview challenged when he takes on an extraordinary task. He agrees to guide a recently freed slave and her mysteriously light-skinned daughter on a dangerous five-day journey across treacherous territory. The central conflict lies in the nature of the girl's horrific curse, as every living organism that comes into physical contact with her mysteriously dies. Her desperate mother is convinced that the girl is harboring a dark, demonic possession that requires spiritual redemption. Conversely, the physician remains steadfast in his scientific beliefs, attributing the lethal phenomenon to an undiscovered physical ailment he deems 'The Sickness.' As they navigate the bloody frontier, they face external threats from ruthless outlaws and harsh wilderness alongside the constant, volatile danger posed by the child herself. The expedition becomes a psychological battleground between faith and medicine, superstition and science. Throughout their journey toward a legendary local Faith Healer, all three travelers are forced to confront their past traumas and personal grief. Ultimately, their path leads them toward an uncertain fate where the boundaries between supernatural horror and medical anomaly blur.",
    "synopsis": "Set in the summer of 1859, 'Killing Faith' is a dark Western thriller that follows a widowed physician struggling with his own grief on the violent American frontier. His routine life is upended when he agrees to accompany a recently freed slave and her Caucasian daughter on a hazardous five-day pilgrimage toward a legendary Faith Healer in a remote town. The young girl carries a terrifying and lethal curse: any living creature she touches perishes instantly. Driven by desperation, her mother believes the affliction is a demonic possession requiring spiritual intervention, while the doctor desperately clings to his scientific background, insisting the deadly touch is the result of a rare pathogen he calls 'The Sickness.' As the trio traverses the blood-soaked landscape, they must survive both the lawless dangers of the West and the chilling peril travelling beside them. The film presents a suspenseful exploration of grief, belief, and survival, pitting cold medical rationale against deep spiritual conviction.",
